Warn: a persisted WORKER reading is restored after a restart only when its account digest (sha256 of the Claude CLI's own orgId and email from auth status, read before and after usage; never stored raw) matches the fresh one, it is within freshnessMs of its original observation, and no CAPACITY_ROLE_INVALIDATED row for that provider and role is at or after it; providers that report no account identity (Codex, Grok) are refused and audited rather than guessed from reset time or registration order
Warn: a capacity row with an unparseable observed_at stored after the newest valid one makes the reading SUSPENDED and the burn unknown, so legacy malformed evidence never lets an older healthy row win; a later valid row replaces it
